active_intake_truth: >
  Content and Improvement contain placeholders only after six exact source artifacts were durably preserved and routed on 2026-08-08. The enterprise goal remains active through the goal system and durable memory. External MemoryEndpoints work and future compressed-vector research remain tracked blockers or planned work, not unprocessed intake files.
current_slice:
  - Integrate `tinyrustlm/tools/vnext-site-publication.js` into the sole current release surface.
  - Bind current site-publisher Ed25519 authority, exact release/source/site/origin scope, expiry, and static readback identity.
  - Generate deterministic forward-only pointer, append-only history, and direct evidence-bound published claim descendants without cyclic ancestry or self-reference.
  - Persist receipts and public subjects create-only after redaction; reconstruct truth from stores and reject caller-provided status, counters, verdicts, or currentness.
  - Cut every maintained caller, command, test helper, configuration path, and architecture document to the vNext replacement.
  - Delete the six obsolete mutable release tools, their dedicated tests, stale maintained documentation, mutable snapshots, aliases, and obsolete schemas without compatibility wrappers or dual readers.
immutable_evidence:
  - The ExactFlat sealed baseline passed only its bounded numerical, controlled-memory, and registered process-crash gates. It is not semantic-memory or product evidence.
  - The frozen TurboVec 0.9.0 four-bit native reference arm is terminally unqualified. Never rerun it, alter its thresholds, or repair its failed process into a pass.
  - Any future compressed-vector arm requires a new preregistration and append-only partial child-process evidence before nonzero-exit rejection.
  - No local fixture, public contract document, or report satisfies authorized MemoryEndpoints individual-account continuity.
engineering_rules:
  - TinyRustLM is pre-release; incur no technical debt and provide no legacy or backward-compatibility support.
  - Rewrite cleanly, remove superseded implementation after verification, and preserve immutable receipts as audit evidence only.
  - Preserve raw failures, fixed seeds, exact identities, bounded allocations, untouched model outputs, and explicit external blockers.
  - Keep static model weights, online KV cache state, durable retrieval vectors, composition graphs, and specialist overlays as separate identity and byte-accounting domains.
  - Do not weaken tests, fabricate live evidence, infer publication from package creation, or infer public reachability from local probes.
  - Keep marketing, documentation, version, release date, last-publish metadata, and per-site update logs synchronized with every stable publication.
next_steps:
  - Inspect the current vNext release surface, site-publication implementation, contracts, tests, callers, and the six obsolete tools before editing.
  - Add the smallest generic failing Gate C tests for any missing sole-path, signature, ancestry, replay, drift, redaction, deterministic-output, and interruption invariant.
  - Implement the replacement and delete obsolete production paths in the same verified cutover; add negative conformance checks forbidding removed imports, commands, documentation, and configuration.
  - Run `npm --prefix tinyrustlm run test:vnext-campaign-release-surface`, `node --test tinyrustlm/tests/vnext-site-publication.test.js`, the complete Node unit gate, Rust fmt, denied-warning Clippy, locked workspace tests, deterministic generator checks, `git diff --check`, and affected browser/deployment tests.
  - Commit and push each coherent green milestone immediately; publish only when affected production closure bytes and their complete independent release gate require it.
  - Continue with Windows directory durability, hostile archive scanning, and protected equality-list custody after Gate C closes.
success_criteria:
  - One release truth path runs from current receipt/subject stores through projection, attestation, preparation, authorization, deployment admission, exact readback, site-publisher authorization, publication descendants, and published-claim admission.
  - Pointer, history, and claim descendants are deterministic, bounded, redacted, forward-only, acyclic, create-only, restart-reconstructable, and bound to current signed authority plus exact deployed bytes.
  - Expired/revoked authority, replay, caller truth injection, source/manifest/snapshot/origin/route/byte drift, cyclic ancestry, generated-document backreferences, partial persistence, and secret-bearing output fail closed.
  - Obsolete mutable tools, tests, commands, stores, schemas, configuration, and maintained documentation are absent, with no alias, shim, migration reader, or dual path.
  - Complete affected tests pass, source is committed/pushed, documentation is synchronized, and no campaign or release claim exceeds current receipts.
